  <description><![CDATA[<!DOCTYPE html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><style>:root{color-scheme:light dark}body{margin:0;padding:12px 16px;font:13px/1.45 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,"Segoe UI",system-ui,sans-serif;color:#1d1d1f;background:#ffffff}h2{font-size:13px;font-weight:600;margin:10px 0 4px}h2:first-child{margin-top:0}ul{margin:0;padding-left:18px}li{margin:2px 0}p{margin:4px 0}code{font:12px ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;background:#f0f0f2;border-radius:4px;padding:0 3px}@media (prefers-color-scheme:dark){body{color:#f5f5f7;background:#1e1e1e}code{background:#2c2c2e}}</style></head><body><h2>What&#x27;s new</h2><ul><li><b>The bee always opens the panel.</b> A click on the bee in the menu bar shows your usage panel, even when the Tiny Hive window is open; it never opens the app instead. Close the panel and the window is back as it was: same size, same place, same page.</li><li><b>Open Tiny Hive is a button.</b> It now sits at the top of the panel, full width, instead of a small link at the bottom.</li></ul></body></html>]]></description>
